<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Waigel - no discussion of EMU criteria in Dublin.</title>
<headline>Waigel - no discussion of EMU criteria in Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Saturday there had been no discussion or challenge to the entry criteria for monetary union at this weekend's meeting of European Union finance ministers.</p>
<p>&quot;There was nobody who wanted to discuss the entry criteria even in the slightest,&quot; he told a briefing at the end of the one-day talks.</p>
<p>The Maastricht Treaty on monetary union sets targets for countries which want to join the single currency, on interest and exchange rates, inflation, budget deficits and public borrowing. -- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 4759258</p>
